{"id": "c5eed363-fb21-47af-b75d-6b0caa2f6c71", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T20:57:52.851782", "source": "user", "parent_id": "a51629f5-5be7-4b03-a5c6-5830f67a069b", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Please inspect the repository at /workspace (structure, README, code under any pipeline/zero-bubble directories, configuration files, existing benchmarks, scripts, and documentation) and report what you find. Then propose an experiment design approach that addresses the stated question about whether 1F1B, 1F1B-I, and ZB-1p throughput improves as microbatch count increases while ZB-2p maintains high throughput with fewer microbatches. The proposal should cover: (1) the independent variables (microbatch count, pipeline depth, method), (2) the dependent variable (throughput) and how it would be measured, (3) controls and constants (model size, batch size, hardware assumptions, warmup/measurement windows), (4) a planned analysis (e.g., curves, comparison framing, statistical handling), and (5) feasibility notes under the design-only constraint. Also list any consequential assumptions or uncertainties you are introducing (e.g., default configuration of the methods, available API surface in the repo, missing details not in the supplied topics). Do NOT produce the full experiment design yet — wait for my review of your proposed approach before continuing.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does the throughput for methods 1F1B, 1F1B-I, and ZB-1p improve as the number of microbatches increases, while ZB-2p maintains high throughput even with fewer microbatches? (Note: These methods are implemented as part of the zero bubble pipeline parallelism strategies in this repository, which aim to reduce pipeline bubbles and maintain high throughput.)\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
